prompt: /home/stack/charon-private/fleet/prompts/tier-recs.md
scope: PRODUCTION-READINESS / setup-UX. A PHASED "tier model recommendations" feature for the
  `charon setup` wizard so a non-expert isn't stuck typing a model name blind. MOTIVATION:
  during `charon setup`, the "model served by X" prompt shows NO list and recommends nothing, so
  a non-expert user has to type a model id from memory with zero guidance (operator dogfood
  observation, charon-vm 2026-06-27). Operator-approved design 2026-06-27.

  PHASES:
  - **Phase A (base layer + fallback) — APPROVED.** At the model-selection prompt, query the
    provider's LIVE `/v1/models` catalog and SHOW it, so the user PICKS from real options instead
    of typing blind. Cheap, never goes stale (it's provider-maintained). Can ship independently
    FIRST; also doubles as the graceful fallback for Phase B. (This is the same "show the live
    model list at the selection prompt" item formerly noted under UX-POLISH — now tracked HERE so
    it isn't double-tracked.)

    **Dogfood evidence (charon-vm 2026-06-27).** Real `charon setup` run (operator): user added
    provider `opencode-zen`, stored the key, imported ALL 49 models into the catalog — but at the
    "model served by '<provider>'" prompt NOTHING was shown, the user hit a blank, and setup
    finished "Done. 0 model(s) configured" → a silently non-functional gateway. This run motivates
    the two requirements below.

    - **Finding 1 (Phase A core).** The just-imported / live catalog must be SURFACED at the
      "model served by X" prompt — it currently shows nothing even right after importing 49 models.
      The import→serve connection must be obvious: after a bulk import, OFFER "serve all N imported? /
      pick from these" rather than leaving a blank prompt. Right now importing into the catalog and
      choosing served models are DISCONNECTED, so a user imports 49 and serves 0.
    - **Finding 2 (correctness guard — QUICK, ship-independently).** If 0 models end up
      configured-to-serve at the end of setup, the wizard must WARN LOUDLY (e.g.
      "⚠ 0 models served — your gateway won't respond to requests") and OFFER to fix it (serve the
      imported catalog / pick some), instead of printing a cheery "Done. 0 model(s) configured."
      This is a quick STANDALONE guard that can ship BEFORE the full recommendation feature.
  - **Phase B (smart layer) — the recommended approach.** After the first provider+key is
    configured, query the provider's live `/models`, then ask 1–3 already-configured / "trusted"
    models to RANK that REAL catalog into Charon's tiers (high / med / low) with fallbacks per
    tier. Surface the recommended models + fallbacks per tier; the user ACCEPTS / adds / removes.
    Query MULTIPLE models and take CONSENSUS for robustness.
    - **CRITICAL anti-hallucination rule:** GROUND the LLM in the live catalog and INTERSECT every
      recommendation with the actual `/models` list — DROP any model the LLM names that isn't
      really in the catalog. This kills training-cutoff staleness and invented/hallucinated model
      ids: only real, currently-served models can ever be recommended.
    - **Sequencing (chicken-and-egg):** Phase B runs AFTER at least one provider+key exists — you
      need a working model to ask.
    - **Sync-first:** fast query + spinner + short timeout. If no model is reachable or the query
      fails → fall back to Phase A (plain live list) → manual entry. TRUE async ("keep setting up
      while it fetches, present recs when ready") = v2 / optional — noted but NOT in the first
      build.
  - **Heuristic fallback (option ii).** When NO model is reachable to ask, INFER tiers from catalog
    metadata — context length / price / name patterns (`70b` / `405b` / `mini` / `flash`) — as an
    offline best-effort.

  CONSTRAINTS: provider/agent-AGNOSTIC; product-clean (no SLOP/fleet/rig leak); affects ONLY the
  setup CONFIG step, NEVER the gateway hot request path; recommendations are ALWAYS
  user-overridable (best-effort, not authoritative). Ties into the existing tier system
  (`tiers.json` / `charon tier`).
note: PARKED — design captured (operator 2026-06-27). Production-readiness-adjacent setup-UX
  feature. Phase A is the cheap immediate win and may ship independently first; Phase B is the
  smart layer (LLM-judge grounded on the live catalog). Activate after charon-vm bringup / when
  setup-UX work is prioritized.

